# ORCLMECH: the self-acting devices — pusher, duplicator, and bomb (M16.4).
#
# These three tick on their own from the moment their board is loaded, which is
# why they cannot live on board 0 the way ORCLPUSH's boulders and ORCLDEV's
# animations do. Board 0 is also the TITLE board, and the adapter's `boot 240`
# span is not a cycle-accurate model of real ZZT booting (oracle/README.md): the
# phase search absorbs that error for anything drawn straight off CurrentTick,
# but never for accumulated state like a duplicator's P1 or a pusher's position.
# So board 0 here is a bare corridor, and every device sits on a board reached
# by walking off a board edge — which, unlike a passage (GAME.PAS:1348), does
# NOT pause the game, so the arriving span is fully modelled on both sides.
#
# The boards are chained east then west so each crossing costs one move:
#   Mech Hub  --east-->  Mech Bay  --west-->  Bomb Bay
#
# Mech Bay, row 8 — the pusher train (ELEMENTS.PAS ElementPusherTick):
#   a front pusher at 11,8 shoves a boulder east down a runway to a solid
#   backstop at 18,8, with a second pusher directly behind it. The trailing
#   pusher is the recursion the tick proc does itself: a pusher that moves looks
#   two squares back along its own step for another pusher facing the same way
#   and ticks it immediately, out of cycle order. When the boulder reaches the
#   backstop the push is refused, and the whole train stops.
#
# Mech Bay, row 13 — the duplicator (ElementDuplicatorTick), source direction
# east, so it reads the gem at 9,13 and writes to 7,13. All four branches:
#   1. destination empty      -> the gem is copied
#   2. destination occupied   -> the occupant is pushed one square first
#   3. the push recurses      -> the whole overflow row shuffles west
#   4. push refused           -> nothing is copied, only the blocked click
#   5. destination is the PLAYER -> the duplicator touches the SOURCE on the
#      player's behalf, so the gem is collected without anyone walking onto it
# A player cannot be the barrier that jams the overflow, because a player is
# Pushable too (ElementDefs[E_PLAYER].Pushable) and is simply shoved along; the
# barrier is the solid wall at 4,13, and the player walks around by row 12.
#
# Bomb Bay — the bomb (ElementBombTick/Touch). Touching an idle bomb arms it
# (P1 := 9); touching an armed one pushes it instead, which is the refusal-side
# station and also moves the blast one square west before it goes off. The two
# explosion phases are DrawPlayerSurroundings(x, y, 1) — damage every
# Destructible tile in the ellipse and fill every empty square with a breakable
# — and phase 2 one bomb cycle later, which clears those breakables again.
# Phase 1 paints its breakables in Random(7) colors, and the oracle's RNG stream
# is not this engine's, so NO checkpoint is taken in the six frames between the
# two phases; what is compared is the board before, and the wreckage after.
# The tiles around the bomb are placed on the ellipse boundary deliberately:
# breakables at dx -7 (49 < 50, erased) and dx -8 (64, survives), and at dy -4
# (32, erased) and dy -5 (50, survives) — so the radius itself is pinned, not
# just the fact that something exploded.
world ORCLMECH
seed 0
phase
boot 240
capture title
play
# Mech Hub: unpause, walk to the east border opening at 60,13 and cross.
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
capture arrive-bay
# The train is already marching down row 8.
settle 24
capture pushers-marching
settle 32
capture pushers-jammed
# Station 1: the first duplication drops a gem on the empty destination.
settle 24
capture dup-copy
# Station 2: the destination is occupied, so its gem is pushed west first.
settle 72
capture dup-push
# Station 3: the push recurses down the overflow squares 6 and 5.
settle 72
capture dup-chain
# Station 4: the overflow reaches the solid barrier at 4,13, so the push is
# refused and nothing is copied — only the blocked click.
settle 72
capture dup-refused
settle 16
# Walk around by row 12 (row 13 is jammed with gems) onto the destination
# square, collecting the gem standing on it.
move right
move up
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move down
capture dup-standing
# Station 5: the destination is the PLAYER, so the duplicator touches the
# SOURCE gem on their behalf — collected without anyone walking onto it.
settle 72
capture dup-touch
# Back out by row 12 and across the west edge into Bomb Bay.
move up
move left
move left
move left
move left
move left
move down
move left
move left
capture arrive-bomb
# Walk up to the bomb at 52,13 and arm it.
move left
move left
move left
move left
move left
move left
move left
move left
capture bomb-armed
# Touching it again pushes it instead: the blast moves one square west.
move left
capture bomb-pushed
# Retreat clear of the ellipse (dx 9 at 60,13) while the fuse burns down.
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
capture bomb-ticking
# Well past both explosion phases: the wreckage, not the fireball.
settle 80
capture bomb-gone
